":true}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000196187","entrez_id":["9725"],"uniprot":["O94886"],"ncbi_summary":"Enables mechanosensitive ion channel activity. Predicted to be involved in cation transmembrane transport. Located in centriolar satellite and lysosomal membrane. Implicated in hypomyelinating leukodystrophy. [provided by Alliance of Genome Resources, Apr 2022]","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"O94886","text":"Mechanosensitive cation channel with low conductance and high activation threshold (PubMed:30382938, PubMed:31587869, PubMed:37543036). In contrast to TMEM63B, does not show phospholipid scramblase activity (PubMed:39716028). Acts as a regulator of lysosomal morphology by mediating lysosomal mechanosensitivity (By similarity). Important for the baby's first breath and respiration throughout life (PubMed:38127458). Upon lung inflation conducts cation currents in alveolar type 1 and 2 cells triggering lamellar body exocytosis and surfactant secretion into airspace (PubMed:38127458). Also acts as an osmosensitive cation channel preferentially activated by hypotonic stress (By similarity)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}